Good — that confirms the plan then: I'll listen for `wheel` events with `ctrlKey: true` (that's exactly how browsers report trackpad pinch and ctrl+scroll to JS) and `preventDefault()` them, so the app handles the zoom instead of the browser's page zoom — same gesture you're already using, just no longer capped by the browser's floor. Plain scroll-wheel gets the same treatment for scroll-mouse users, and real touchscreen pinch needs separate distance-tracking since browsers don't route that through `wheel` events. Let me implement this, scoped to Sandbox first (where "seeing the full audible range" actually matters).


